<%# Article-history pilot: the article's identifier on a line of its own (HistoryPilotHelper#history_identifier), first
    in the article's frame whenever the article shows anything but its plain text (laws/_history_article). It is set in
    the type of the legal text (ReferencesHelper::ARTICLE_CONTENT_CLASSES), so it stands exactly where the wording's own
    number stands in the plain text: the panel opening below it, a step and Close leave it in place (the owner, via Sol
    2026-11-23 04:31:08Z). It is the button that opens the article's menu (article_copy_menu_controller.js makes it
    one), so History and the copies stay at hand (Sol 2026-11-21 10:09:36Z: a visible, keyboard-operable identifier
    outside the diff).
    Locals: identifier. %>
<div class="<%= ReferencesHelper::ARTICLE_CONTENT_CLASSES %>" data-history-identifier><span class="article-number not-prose cursor-pointer"><%= identifier %></span></div>
